# TestRail > Shortcut checklist

Whenever you **create** (or ACC-write) TestRail case(s) for a Shortcut story:

## Required

1. `addCase` first. Then add the new cases to the **progression or named test run** (merge only).
2. Resolve each new case to its **run test instance** via `get_tests` on that run (`case_id` > `id`).
3. **Immediately** add a Shortcut checklist task on that story (`stories-add-task`).
4. **One checklist item per case** (do not batch multiple IDs into one task).
5. **Format (permanent):**

```text
qa test: <TESTRAIL_BASE_URL>/index.php?/tests/view/<testId>
```

Use the **test** in the progression/test run, not the suite case. That URL is the result page (Passed / Failed / Retest).

Resolve `<TESTRAIL_BASE_URL>` from project-context, prefs, or MCP config (never hardcode a company host in this rule).

Example shape:

```text
qa test: https://your-org.testrail.io/index.php?/tests/view/12345
```

## Plan / run merge (do not rewrite)

- Load existing case IDs from `get_tests` on the run, never from `get_plan` (runs lack `case_ids`).
- `update_plan_entry` **replaces** the run set. IDs omitted from the payload are dropped and **their results are wiped**.
- Always merge: existing run case IDs + new case IDs. Never send only the new IDs. Never use `-NoMerge` unless the user explicitly asks to replace the run.
- After merge, verify `get_tests` count (before + new, unless the user asked to remove cases).

## Never

- Suite case links (`cases/view/<caseId>`) on the QA execution checklist
- Suite/section links (`suites/view/...&group_id=...`)
- Run section group links (`runs/view/...&group_id=...`)
- Checklist before the case is on the run (no test instance yet)

## Flow

`addCase` (get `caseId`) > merge onto the progression/test run > `get_tests` (get `testId`) > `stories-add-task` with `tests/view/<testId>` in the same turn as the TestRail write.
